# Cloudflare's, for every file it serves of deploy/site/ (wrangler.jsonc):
# the bridge's build, which deploy/stage.js places there, writing this beside
# it as deploy/site/_headers. Cloudflare reads that and doesn't serve it.
# What no file answers, deploy/worker.js does, with the same but its own
# policy, as its answers are no pages.
#
# The Content-Security-Policy is the one the build's page carries
# (vite.config.js, from scripts/csp.js), which stage.js puts in place of
# PAGE_POLICY: the bridge's own scripts alone, WebAssembly, what the bridge
# reads from, and frame-ancestors, which a page's own policy can't say.
/*
  Strict-Transport-Security: max-age=31536000
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
  Content-Security-Policy: PAGE_POLICY
  X-Frame-Options: DENY

/assets/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=31536000, immutable
